.TH INTENT-GUI 1 "2026-10-26" "intent-gui 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
intent-gui \- keyboard-first, local-first task management (GPUI application)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B intent-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B intent-gui
is the desktop interface for Intent: an opinionated, keyboard-first task
manager with a Vim-like interaction model. It shares the same SQLite database
as the
.BR intent (1)
CLI and reloads within two seconds when the database changes externally.
.PP
The window has four surfaces: the task list, the task editor (title + notes,
full Vim editing), prompts (capture, defer, due, remind, organize, search,
commands), and a help overlay.
.SS Keymap essentials
.TP
.B j k gg G ctrl-d ctrl-u
move
.TP
.B 1 2 3 4 " (or " alt+1 ".." alt+5" ")"
switch view (inbox / today / upcoming / completed; alt+5 = archived —
bare digits 5-9 start counts)
.TP
.B tab
cycle views
.TP
.BR o " / " "space space"
capture
.TP
.BR enter " / " i " / " a
edit task
.TP
.BR ctrl+j " / " ctrl+k
switch between title and notes (both modes)
.TP
.B x
complete / reopen / revive
.TP
.BR "space d" " / " "space u" " / " "space r"
defer / due / remind prompts
.TP
.B "space o"
organize
.TP
.B "space t"
tag prompt: +add / \-remove tokens
.TP
.B "space f"
filter prompt: apply a project/tag lens over the current view; the sidebar
lists projects and tags with counts (clicking toggles; an active lens row
shows visible/total; esc clears)
.TP
.B "space D"
unarchive
.TP
.B "space p"
paste the system clipboard (editor)
.TP
.B > <
shift due by a day
.TP
.B + \-
raise / lower priority
.TP
.B V
visual (multi-task) mode
.TP
.BR d " / " "space D"
archive / unarchive
.TP
.B D
delete \(em press twice; the row turns red while armed (session-undoable)
.TP
.BR y " / " Y
yank title / title+notes
.TP
.BR u " / " "ctrl-r"
undo / redo task operations
.TP
.B .
repeat last operation
.TP
.B /
search \(em live; matches highlight as you type,
.B n
/
.B N
cycle matches
.TP
.B :
command prompt
.TP
.B ?
help overlay
.PP
Key sequences never time out; pending keys are always visible in the status
line and
.B escape
cancels. Deleting text never clobbers the system clipboard.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.local/share/intent/tasks.db
(default database; override with
.BR $INTENT_DB )
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR intent (1)
